      "text": "## The Exploration-Exploitation Dilemma"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:04-model-free-control, git-history:reinforcement-learning:04-model-free-control]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md",
        "concepts": "[sarsa, q-learning, on-policy, off-policy, exploration, epsilon-greedy, UCB, optimism]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:model-free-control",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[q-learning, on-policy, off-policy]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Model-Free Control - SARSA, Q-Learning, Exploration",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "To act greedily you must know `q` — but to learn `q` you must try actions that\nlook suboptimal. If you only ever take the current-best action you never discover\na better one. This is the exploration-exploitation trade-off, and it has no\nanalogue in supervised learning."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md#008",
      "path": [
        "04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:reinforcement-learning:04-model-free-control, git-history:reinforcement-learning:04-model-free-control]",
        "canonical_path": "reinforcement-learning/04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md",
        "concepts": "[sarsa, q-learning, on-policy, off-policy, exploration, epsilon-greedy, UCB, optimism]",
        "current_path": "reinforcement-learning/04-MODEL-FREE-CONTROL.md",
        "id": "maxim:reinforcement-learning:model-free-control",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "reinforcement-learning",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[q-learning, on-policy, off-policy]",
        "section": "reinforcement-learning",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Model-Free Control - SARSA, Q-Learning, Exploration",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  EXPLOIT                          EXPLORE                        |\n|  -------                          -------                        |\n|  take argmax_a Q(s,a)             try other actions to learn     |\n|  maximize reward NOW              improve Q for the future       |\n|  risk: stuck in a local optimum   risk: wasted reward now        |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
